## Lore

The Flame Cloud is a flying assault cyborg built like a serpent or a true
dragon. It has the most advanced flight system the Republic of Japan can build
and no wings at all: at the near-supersonic speeds it reaches, wings would only
add stress. It is very fast, but only maneuverable once it drops to moderate
speeds.

Its name comes from its favorite attack, a swooping dive with a long blast of
plasma flame from the mouth. Lasers on its jet thrusters and twin particle
beam cannons on its tail complete its armament. Flame Clouds often fly beside
SAMAS and other flying power armor; a common tactic is to send one or two to
strafe jungle or forest and flush out monsters and demons for more heavily
armed troops to finish.

Like every dragon ''borg, the pilot volunteered to become a Republic cyborg
soldier, and in the Republic a ''borg is a hero rather than a monster. But the
body is so inhuman that few volunteers are placed in it.

## GM Notes

Standard military issue is all the ammunition and equipment the body needs,
an energy rifle, four extra E-clips, four grenades, distancing binoculars, a
utility belt, a backpack, a walkie-talkie and regular maintenance and repairs.
A jet pack, hover vehicle, extra weapons and equipment are available on
assignment, at the local commander''s discretion. The character has medium
security clearance to most military bases, hospitals and facilities.

Pay is a 2000 credit monthly salary with room, board and basic needs provided;
officers of 9th level and higher get 3500 to 5000 a month, and police ''borgs 800
more than an unaugmented officer. Rank is standard military, private to
general.

A decommissioned ''borg may keep basic bionics as a registered citizen, keep
most of its systems after long or distinguished service if it leaves for
private security or the wilderness (surrendering citizenship in the latter
case), or be retro-fitted into a bio-system or clone body. A full conversion
''borg with regular maintenance could stay active for 300 years or more.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-flame-cloud');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dragon-borg-flame-cloud';

